# Preload hardened_malloc for every dynamically linked process, including
# Flatpak apps (their sandbox shares the host's /etc/ld.so.preload).
#
# hardened_malloc makes the allocator safe against heap corruption, which is
# the bug class most memory-safety issues in a browser end up being. See
# https://github.com/anthonyharrison/hardened_malloc
#
# It costs some allocator throughput. On an i5-3550 that is measurable in
# allocator-heavy work, so `with-standard-malloc COMMAND` runs any command
# with the stock glibc allocator instead:
#
#     with-standard-malloc ./benchmark
#
# Note: LD_PRELOAD entries here are ignored for setuid binaries, which is the
# correct behaviour.
/usr/lib64/libhardened_malloc.so
